Rationale (brief): The run diagnostics and Analyzer both show exploration objectives (distance_from_center mean=0.400739, parameter_spread mean=0.397121) are strongly improved while performance is effectively zero (performance mean=0.000305, best=0.00045 — down from a prior best 0.011353). This is consistent with objective-weighting causing selection pressure away from performance. Changing the performance objective weight is the simplest, low-risk, and directly targeted intervention to restore exploitation and test whether performance can be recovered (if the scorer itself is broken, this change will quickly show no improvement and we can then pursue implementation diagnostics).

